  "summary": "pypdf has possible large memory usage when parsing cross-reference streams",
  "details": "### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory usage. This requires opening a file with cross-reference streams.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.21.3](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.21.3).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#4269](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/4269).",
